# DexCompare (sealed) — copy to .env for local development.

# Postgres. In Vercel: the Neon POOLED connection string (host contains "-pooler").
# In the GitHub Actions secret DEXCOMPARE_SEALED_DATABASE_URL: the DIRECT string.
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://postgres:postgres@127.0.0.1:5432/dexsealed"

# Canonical site origin, no trailing slash. Used in canonical URLs, the sitemap
# and email links.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL="https://dexcompare.app"

# Shared secret between the import job and /api/revalidate. Any long random string:
#   node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('hex'))"
REVALIDATE_SECRET=""

# Optional.
NEXT_PUBLIC_CONTACT_EMAIL="riftcompare@gmail.com"
NEXT_PUBLIC_EBAY_CAMPAIGN_ID="5339155912"
NEXT_PUBLIC_TCGPLAYER_IMPACT_LINK="https://partner.tcgplayer.com/c/7385758/1780961/21018"
GOOGLE_SITE_VERIFICATION=""

# Google AdSense (DEPLOY.md, "Google AdSense"). Read at build time: redeploy after changing. Empty = no Google script at all.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ADSENSE_CLIENT="pub-1234567890123456"
# The guides' in-article ad unit (AdSense → Ads → By ad unit → In-article → its data-ad-slot number).
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ADSENSE_SLOT_GUIDE=""

# eBay listing strips. The website holds NO eBay credential: the listings are imported once a day by
# scripts/ebay-import.ts (GitHub Actions: secrets EBAY_CLIENT_ID and EBAY_CLIENT_SECRET, DexCompare's OWN Production
# keyset; see DEPLOY.md, "eBay listings: the daily import"). To run the importer locally, export them in the shell
# (tsx does not read .env) together with DATABASE_URL:
#   EBAY_CLIENT_ID=... EBAY_CLIENT_SECRET=... npx tsx scripts/ebay-import.ts --dry-run
# Read by the website (Vercel) and, for the purge, by the import jobs:
# Kill switch: "off" makes the route answer empty (the strips become the plain search row).
# EBAY_LISTINGS=off
# How old a listing may be before it is never shown (hours, default 26; 5.5 = eBay's six-hour rule with margin).
# EBAY_LISTING_MAX_AGE_HOURS=26
# The importer only (GitHub variables): daily call cap (2500, also the max: this site's share of a 5,000 keyset shared with the
# owner's other site; set EBAY_DAILY_CAP on BOTH sites) and per-run cap (2500, a strict ceiling on searches INCLUDING retries;
# set it lower to keep room for a manual re-run the same Pacific day).
# EBAY_DAILY_CAP=2500
# EBAY_RUN_CAP=2500
# Calls the catalogue sweep may spend per run (broad searches, 200 listings a call, each listing handed to the product it is);
# per-product searches get what it leaves. A repository variable; the workflow passes it to the importer.
# EBAY_SWEEP_CALLS=2100
# Compliant mode (six hours): EBAY_LISTING_MAX_AGE_HOURS=5.5 here AND as a GitHub variable, EBAY_RUN_CAP=380, and the cron in
# .github/workflows/dexcompare-ebay-import.yml set to "13 */4 * * *" (DEPLOY.md, "The switch to compliant mode").
